TITLE: The export-backed Perspective explorer renders and restores a query

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[EVIDENCE]
UID: EV-SDOC-PERSPECTIVE-FIRST-EXPLORER
TITLE: The export-backed Perspective explorer renders and restores a query
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
SOURCE: StrictDoc 0.28.3 JSON export; Perspective 5.3.0 CDN build; headless Chromium; codex spike contracts; 2026-08-31
STATEMENT: >>>
A direct request exported 372 documents and 372 nodes with 954 relations from
a 9,162,301-byte json/index.json in 2,171.6 ms, then returned 372 flat rows
without retaining the export. Headless Chromium defined the Perspective custom
element, rendered its Pro Dark Datagrid with the native settings panel and
eight selected columns, and reported the same node and relation counts. A
native _NODE_TYPE group-by survived a fresh-export page reload through the
viewer's save and restore token. The browser smoke exposed a blocked
Perspective blob module under the initial Content-Security-Policy; the final
policy admits blob scripts and workers while retaining the remaining
restrictions.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Measured on the codex spike branch (feat/strictdoc-trial-codex) before the
merge; ported 2026-09-01 because two findings still govern the merged app: the
CSP directive set, kept verbatim in server.py, and the per-request export cost
that DEC-SDOC-BOARD-READS-THE-SCRIBE-DAEMON removes. The spike's test file did
not survive the merge, so this carries no File relation.
<<<
